Nexpath is an Augmented Reality Navigation mobile app designed to help students, staff, and visitors find their way around campus departmental buildings.
Think of it like Google Maps, but instead of just showing you a map, it uses your phone’s camera to recognize your surroundings and display arrows on your screen showing you which direction to go.
You simply search for where you want to go, select the destination, and follow the AR directions until you arrive.
To try it go to https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1wSxujMYtNmuEXM7f_rUokA-lFAZ-s5rg?zx=nhn9s9oe67s6 and download and launch the apk on your mobile phone but first make sure your device is compatible with Google services for AR.
